-","gene_id":"ENSG00000134049","module":"turquoise","kme":0.154977,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.787198,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Vascular.niche","gene_id":"ENSG00000134049","module":"black","kme":0.225199,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.104801,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000134049","entrez_id":["51124"],"uniprot":["Q9Y5U9"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a small protein that is localized to the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) and may play a role in the ER stress response by mediating cell differentiation and apoptosis. Transcription of this gene is regulated by tumor necrosis factor alpha and specificity protein 1 (Sp1). Mutations in this gene may play a role in microcephaly, epilepsy, and diabetes syndrome (MEDS), and a pseudogene of this gene is located on the long arm of chromosome 12. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y5U9","text":"Regulator of endoplasmic reticulum secretion that acts as a key determinant of brain size (PubMed:33122427). Required for secretion of extracellular matrix proteins (PubMed:33122427). Required for correct brain development by depositing sufficient extracellular matrix proteins for tissue integrity and the proliferation of neural progenitors (PubMed:33122427). Acts as a regulator of the unfolded protein response (UPR) (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}